h=3D"">Let=E2=80=99s look at the common architecture pattern of the API gat=
eway. Here we have a single, public facing API that sits in front of many o=
ther APIs. It knows how to route to them, and it may be that it=E2=80=99s t=
he only service that can route to them. You=E2=80=99ll see this kind of pat=
tern often used when using microservices and in cloud services such as Azur=
e Service Fabric.</p><figure class=3D"nf ng nh ni nj nk nc nd paragraph-ima=
